    "wl_tabbed_image_and_text_EzzGVE": {
      "type": "wl-tabbed-image-and-text",
      "name": "HL Tabbed Image & Text",
      "settings": {
        "cclasses": "",
        "color": "#eae1d5",
        "font_color": "#241f21",
        "link_color": "#C83D1B",
        "show_tab": true,
        "tab_color": "#ffffff",
        "margin_top": 68,
        "margin_bottom": 68,
        "title": "Sourced for Absorption. Combined for Potency.",
        "max_width": 94,
        "content": "<p>We formulate with whole-plant, <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/collections/full-spectrum-whole-plant-cbd\" target=\"_blank\">full-spectrum hemp extracts</a> rather than isolated single compounds. The reason is biological: cannabinoids, terpenes, and flavonoids appear to work more effectively together than in isolation—a phenomenon researchers refer to as the entourage effect. A full-spectrum extract preserves the plant’s natural chemical diversity, delivering a broader range of active compounds in every serving.<br/><br/>Where individual cannabinoid isolates strip the plant down to one molecule, our approach retains the supporting cast—minor cannabinoids like CBG and CBC, aromatic terpenes, and plant-derived flavonoids—that research suggests may enhance overall efficacy. For a deeper look at how these compounds interact, see <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/pages/what-are-cannabinoids\" target=\"_blank\">What Are Cannabinoids?</a></p>",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/sourced-for-absorption.png",
        "image_position": "left"
      }
    },
    "wl_tabbed_image_and_text_FECw6m": {
      "type": "wl-tabbed-image-and-text",
      "name": "HL Tabbed Image & Text",
      "settings": {
        "cclasses": "",
        "color": "#ffffff",
        "font_color": "#241f21",
        "link_color": "#C83D1B",
        "show_tab": true,
        "tab_color": "#eae1d5",
        "margin_top": 68,
        "margin_bottom": 68,
        "title": "Core Carrier: Organic MCT Oil",
        "max_width": 58,
        "content": "<p>Cannabinoids are lipophilic—they dissolve in fats, not water. On their own, oral CBD has been estimated to have a bioavailability of just 13–19%. That means without a proper carrier, most of what you ingest never reaches systemic circulation.<br/><br/>Medium-chain triglycerides (MCTs), derived from organic coconut oil, serve as the delivery vehicle in our oil-based tinctures. MCTs are rapidly digested and absorbed compared to longer-chain fats, facilitating faster transport of cannabinoids into the bloodstream. Published research confirms that lipid-based formulations—including those using MCT—significantly improve the oral delivery of CBD compared to lipid-free preparations (<a href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10892205/\" target=\"_blank\">PMC – Strategies to Improve CBD Bioavailability</a>). MCT oil also demonstrates superior terpene preservation during storage, helping maintain the full-spectrum profile over the product’s shelf life. Explore our <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/products/organic-cbd-full-spectrum-mct-oil\" target=\"_blank\">CBD MCT Oil tinctures →</a></p>",
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/Core_Carrier.png",
        "image_position": "left"
      }
    },
    "wl_hierarchy_UcptpM": {
      "type": "wl-hierarchy",
      "blocks": {
        "card_eDR4Cx": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "shopify://shop_images/1_icon_small_b9d675e8-1d87-4335-a00d-72e6ebd37234.png",
            "header": "Cannabinoids",
            "header_color": "#bcd868",
            "header_font_color": "#241f21",
            "body_color": "#fcf5ed",
            "content": "<p><strong>CBD (Cannabidiol): </strong>The primary non-intoxicating cannabinoid in hemp. Commonly discussed for its potential role in supporting calm and physical comfort. <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/blogs/blog/how-does-cbd-work\" target=\"_blank\">Learn how CBD works →</a></p><p><strong>CBN (Cannabinol):</strong> A minor cannabinoid formed as THC ages. Commonly discussed for its association with relaxation and restful sleep.<a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/pages/what-is-cbn\" target=\"_blank\">Learn more about CBN →</a></p><p><strong>CBG (Cannabigerol):</strong> Known as the “mother cannabinoid”—the biosynthetic precursor to CBD, THC, and CBC. Commonly discussed for focus and digestive comfort.</p><p><strong>CBC (Cannabichromene): </strong>A non-intoxicating cannabinoid that interacts with TRP channel receptors rather than CB1/CB2 directly. Commonly discussed for its contribution to the entourage effect.</p>"
          }
        },
        "card_cFaqiy": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "shopify://shop_images/2_icon_small_b7be1836-5ee9-42e8-aa9c-d7ccb8b56eda.png",
            "header": "Terpenes",
            "header_color": "#595378",
            "header_font_color": "#ffffff",
            "body_color": "#fcf5ed",
            "content": "<p>Terpenes are aromatic compounds found across the plant kingdom—not unique to hemp. In full-spectrum extracts, they contribute to flavor, aroma, and may modulate how cannabinoids interact with the body. Key terpenes preserved in our extracts include:</p><p><strong>Myrcene: </strong>The most abundant terpene in cannabis. Also found in hops, lemongrass, and mangoes. Commonly discussed for its calming and muscle-relaxing properties.</p><p><strong>Limonene: </strong>Found in citrus peels. Commonly discussed for mood elevation and stress relief.</p><p><strong>Pinene: </strong>Found in pine needles and rosemary. Commonly discussed for alertness and respiratory support.<br/>For more on terpene science, visit our <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/blogs/blog/benefits-of-terpenes\" target=\"_blank\">benefits of terpenes guide</a>.</p>"
          }
        },
        "card_zdbqpA": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "shopify://shop_images/3_icon_small_9cff19d8-73b4-4bf5-805b-9937bdbcb4ee.png",
            "header": "Flavonoids",
            "header_color": "#e57e3b",
            "header_font_color": "#241f21",
            "body_color": "#fcf5ed",
            "content": "<p>Flavonoids are polyphenolic compounds with documented antioxidant properties. Hemp-specific flavonoids—sometimes called d—are present in small quantities in whole-plant extracts and are retained in our full-spectrum formulations.</p><p>This same cannabinoid, terpene, and flavonoid profile carries into our animal formulas, where the <a href=\"https://hemplucid.com/collections/pets-cbd\" target=\"_blank\">pet cbd oil ingredients</a> are held to identical sourcing standards at concentrations calibrated for smaller body weights.</p><p></p>"
          }
        }
      },
